  "json.parse": "```flame\njson.fn parse(string: String) -> Object\n```\n\nParses a JSON string into a Flame value (formula/object, tuple/array, string, number, boolean, or nil).\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet obj = json.parse(\"{\\\"name\\\": \\\"Flame\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.6.0\\\"}\")\nprintln(obj.name)\n```",
  "std.json.parse": "```flame\njson.fn parse(string: String) -> Object\n```\n\nParses a JSON string into a Flame value (formula/object, tuple/array, string, number, boolean, or nil).\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet obj = json.parse(\"{\\\"name\\\": \\\"Flame\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.6.0\\\"}\")\nprintln(obj.name)\n```",
  "parse": "```flame\njson.fn parse(string: String) -> Object\n```\n\nParses a JSON string into a Flame value (formula/object, tuple/array, string, number, boolean, or nil).\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet obj = json.parse(\"{\\\"name\\\": \\\"Flame\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.6.0\\\"}\")\nprintln(obj.name)\n```",
  "json.fromJson": "```flame\njson.fn fromJson(data: Unknown) -> Object\n```\n\nParses JSON from either a String or a raw byte buffer (Bytes).\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet raw_bytes = [0x7b, 0x22, 0x61, 0x22, 0x3a, 0x31, 0x7d]\nlet data = json.fromJson(raw_bytes)\nprintln(data.a)\n```",
  "std.json.fromJson": "```flame\njson.fn fromJson(data: Unknown) -> Object\n```\n\nParses JSON from either a String or a raw byte buffer (Bytes).\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet raw_bytes = [0x7b, 0x22, 0x61, 0x22, 0x3a, 0x31, 0x7d]\nlet data = json.fromJson(raw_bytes)\nprintln(data.a)\n```",
  "fromJson": "```flame\njson.fn fromJson(data: Unknown) -> Object\n```\n\nParses JSON from either a String or a raw byte buffer (Bytes).\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet raw_bytes = [0x7b, 0x22, 0x61, 0x22, 0x3a, 0x31, 0x7d]\nlet data = json.fromJson(raw_bytes)\nprintln(data.a)\n```",
  "json.read": "```flame\njson.fn read(filepath: String) -> Object\n```\n\nHigh-performance streaming JSON file reader that deserializes directly from a disk file path without loading the raw string into memory.\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet dataset = json.read(\"benchmark.json\")\nprintln(dataset.users.len())\n```",
  "std.json.read": "```flame\njson.fn read(filepath: String) -> Object\n```\n\nHigh-performance streaming JSON file reader that deserializes directly from a disk file path without loading the raw string into memory.\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet dataset = json.read(\"benchmark.json\")\nprintln(dataset.users.len())\n```",
  "json.stringify": "```flame\njson.fn stringify(value: Unknown, pretty: Bool = false) -> String\n```\n\nSerializes a Flame value into a JSON formatted string. Optionally pass `pretty: true` for 2-space indented output.\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet compact = json.stringify(data)\nlet pretty = json.stringify(data, true)\n```",
  "std.json.stringify": "```flame\njson.fn stringify(value: Unknown, pretty: Bool = false) -> String\n```\n\nSerializes a Flame value into a JSON formatted string. Optionally pass `pretty: true` for 2-space indented output.\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet compact = json.stringify(data)\nlet pretty = json.stringify(data, true)\n```",
  "stringify": "```flame\njson.fn stringify(value: Unknown, pretty: Bool = false) -> String\n```\n\nSerializes a Flame value into a JSON formatted string. Optionally pass `pretty: true` for 2-space indented output.\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet compact = json.stringify(data)\nlet pretty = json.stringify(data, true)\n```",
  "json.write": "```flame\njson.fn write(filepath: String, value: Unknown, pretty: Bool = false) -> Bool\n```\n\nSerializes a Flame value directly into a destination file on disk. Optionally formats with indentation if `pretty: true`.\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet success = json.write(\"output.json\", data, true)\n```",
  "std.json.write": "```flame\njson.fn write(filepath: String, value: Unknown, pretty: Bool = false) -> Bool\n```\n\nSerializes a Flame value directly into a destination file on disk. Optionally formats with indentation if `pretty: true`.\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nlet success = json.write(\"output.json\", data, true)\n```",
  "json.valid": "```flame\njson.fn valid(string: String) -> Bool\n```\n\nQuickly validates whether a string contains valid JSON syntax without allocating memory or building an in-memory object tree.\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nif json.valid(raw_str) {\n    let val = json.parse(raw_str)\n}\n```",
  "std.json.valid": "```flame\njson.fn valid(string: String) -> Bool\n```\n\nQuickly validates whether a string contains valid JSON syntax without allocating memory or building an in-memory object tree.\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nif json.valid(raw_str) {\n    let val = json.parse(raw_str)\n}\n```",
  "valid": "```flame\njson.fn valid(string: String) -> Bool\n```\n\nQuickly validates whether a string contains valid JSON syntax without allocating memory or building an in-memory object tree.\n\n**Example:**\n```flame\nimport std.json\n\nif json.valid(raw_str) {\n    let val = json.parse(raw_str)\n}\n```",
